## 12. Acceptance Checklist

- [ ] Covers every required screen.
- [ ] Keeps P0 and P1 boundaries visible.
- [ ] Does not include forbidden copy or out-of-scope entry points.
- [ ] Uses realistic, buildable UI patterns.
- [ ] Provides enough component/state detail for visual design.
- [ ] Can be handed to Figma without reading the full PRD.
- [ ] Identifies existing component instances, variable bindings and Auto Layout/responsive constraints.
- [ ] Records design-search evidence and its mapping to the current Fenleng theme and typography/density profiles.
- [ ] Names concrete screenshot/viewports/state checks; distinguishes a prompt review from an executed Figma visual review.

